/-!
# Uniform constants for the canonical initial-variable adjoint

The normal-symbol, compact regularization, literal adjoint limit and supported
expansion estimates choose their constants before the varying phase, chart,
rescaling, amplitude and trade fields. They retain the original measures and the
reserve `2*(n+1)` in `app:ch_background:prop:bg-adjoint`.

`UniformEndpoint.exists_uniform_scalarTransportCarrierAdjoint_periodic_raw_bound`
chooses the constant from fixed physical localization, support sets, geometry
budgets and nonnegative profiles before the carrier, conic maps and rescaling,
scalar, flow, normal, trade fields, high budget and datum. It constructs the
literal periodic adjoint with full raw Sobolev membership and the additive bound
at every natural order, including zero.

Finite syntactic expansion profiles, the exact expansion length, joint Fourier
interpolation, compact-test summation, density extension and periodic transfer
discharge all intermediate operator estimates. The original measures, Fourier
normalization, half-order amplitude and reserve `2*(n+1)` are retained. Actual
canonical profile and geometry instantiation remains with `Canonical.LocalAdjoint`
and its parent construction.
-/
